     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"The target is not reachable. Entry nodes edge0 and edge1 still reach h1_0, h1_2, h2_0 and h2_2, and h2_2 leads on to h4_1. However, every route to crown:obtain depends on a blocked step. h3_0 is an AND step that needs h1_1, which is blocked, so h3_0 is cut off. h3_1 needs h1_1 and h3_2 needs h2_1, so both are cut off. That leaves h4_0 (needs h3_0) and h4_2 (needs h3_0 or h2_1) unreachable. As a result h5_0 (needs h4_0, h4_2 or h3_1), h5_1 (needs h3_0) and h5_2 (needs h3_2) are all unreachable. With none of its parents reachable, crown:obtain cannot be reached.\"}"
    }
